1. Embedded Write &amp; Read (bbolt) <pre><code>&lt;pipeline description="Embedded KV Operations Example"
          xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
          xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/etl-madness/flow/main/xsd/pipeline.xsd"&gt;
    &lt;variables&gt;
        &lt;variable name="CACHE_FILE" type="string" value="./data/pipeline.db" /&gt;
        &lt;variable name="USER_ID" type="string" value="usr_9901" /&gt;
        &lt;variable name="USER_DATA" type="string" value='{"status":"active","tier":"gold"}' /&gt;
    &lt;/variables&gt;

    &lt;databases&gt;
        &lt;database name="embedded_store" driver="bbolt" connection_string="{{CACHE_FILE}}" /&gt;
    &lt;/databases&gt;

    &lt;flow&gt;
        &lt;!-- Write record to "user_sessions" bucket --&gt;
        &lt;kv id="write_session" 
            db="embedded_store" 
            bucket="user_sessions" 
            op="put" 
            key="{{USER_ID}}" 
            value="{{USER_DATA}}" /&gt;

        &lt;!-- Read record from "user_sessions" bucket into variable "RETRIEVED_SESSION" --&gt;
        &lt;kv id="read_session" 
            db="embedded_store" 
            bucket="user_sessions" 
            op="get" 
            key="{{USER_ID}}" 
            output_var="RETRIEVED_SESSION" /&gt;

        &lt;!-- Output assertion --&gt;
        &lt;assert id="check_session" var="RETRIEVED_SESSION" operator="ne" value="" /&gt;
    &lt;/flow&gt;
&lt;/pipeline&gt;
</code></pre>

2. Inline Command DSL Usage <p>You can supply key-value commands using inline text body instead of XML attributes: <pre><code>&lt;pipeline xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
          xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/etl-madness/flow/main/xsd/pipeline.xsd"&gt;
    &lt;flow&gt;
    &lt;!-- Inline PUT command --&gt;
    &lt;kv id="inline_write" db="embedded_store" bucket="config"&gt;
        PUT system_status operational
    &lt;/kv&gt;

    &lt;!-- Inline GET command --&gt;
    &lt;kv id="inline_read" db="embedded_store" bucket="config" output_var="SYS_STATUS"&gt;
        GET system_status
    &lt;/kv&gt;
    &lt;/flow&gt;
&lt;/pipeline&gt;
</code></pre></p>

3. Key Prefix Scanning <pre><code>&lt;pipeline xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
          xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/etl-madness/flow/main/xsd/pipeline.xsd"&gt;
    &lt;flow&gt;
        &lt;!-- Scan all keys starting with 'usr_' in the 'accounts' bucket --&gt;
        &lt;kv id="scan_users" 
            db="embedded_store" 
            bucket="accounts" 
            op="scan" 
            key="usr_" 
            output_var="USER_LIST" /&gt;
    &lt;/flow&gt;
&lt;/pipeline&gt;
</code></pre>

4. High-Performance Bulk ETL (PostgreSQL to bbolt) <p>Stream 100,000+ user records directly from PostgreSQL into a local bbolt embedded database chunked in batches of 5,000 records.</p> <pre><code>&lt;pipeline description="PostgreSQL to bbolt Streaming ETL"
          xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
          xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/etl-madness/flow/main/xsd/pipeline.xsd"&gt;
    &lt;databases&gt;
        &lt;database name="postgres_db" driver="postgres" connection_string="postgres://user:pass@localhost:5432/app?sslmode=disable" /&gt;
        &lt;database name="cache_db" driver="bbolt" connection_string="./cache/lookup.db" /&gt;
    &lt;/databases&gt;

    &lt;flow&gt;
        &lt;!-- The SQL query MUST return at least 2 columns: Column 1 = Key, Column 2 = Value --&gt;
        &lt;kv_bulk id="cache_user_tokens" 
                 db="postgres_db" 
                 target_db="cache_db" 
                 target_bucket="tokens" 
                 batch_size="5000" 
                 output_var="COPIED_COUNT"&gt;
            SELECT 
                user_id AS key, 
                auth_token AS value 
            FROM active_user_tokens 
            WHERE is_valid = true
        &lt;/kv_bulk&gt;

        &lt;assert id="verify_bulk_transfer" var="COPIED_COUNT" operator="ne" value="0" /&gt;
    &lt;/flow&gt;
&lt;/pipeline&gt;
</code></pre>

